  "description": "The neuroscience concentration in chemistry or biochemistry seeks to provide students with an interdisciplinary understanding of neuroscience, giving them a deep understanding of the chemical sciences and integrating this knowledge with subject areas as diverse as psychology, biology, physics, computer science, and philosophy. This training prepares students for graduate school in neuroscience and professional fields (e.g., medicine, dentistry, clinical psychology, veterinary medicine, physical therapy), as well as careers in biotechnology firms, government laboratories, pharmaceutical companies, education, law, and business.",
